/*
  Added to address the issue where session timeout login dialog had double scrollbars (SVF-1557).
  Even though iframe height is 100% of binf-modal-body, it is triggering overflow in binf-modal-body becasue of descenders.
  Descenders are extra white space at bottom of all inline-elements and iframes are also by default are rendered as inline-element.
  Stackoverflow link for further explaination: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36974514/why-is-there-a-vertical-scroll-bar-if-parent-and-child-have-the-same-height

  This is default behaviour of browser and below fix is just for session timeout login dialog,
  below css will mark login iframe as block element which would remove descenders causing the issue.
  This is a very edge case scenario where parent has overflow enabled and child is an inline-element with 100% height of parent.
  Any other leading application facing same issue should be fixed from leading application side only.
*/
.binf-widgets .binf-modal-dialog.binf-modal-full .binf-modal-body iframe {
  display: block;
}

